{"type":"standard","title":"Darren Bailey","displaytitle":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Darren Bailey</span></span>","namespace":{"id":0,"text":""},"wikibase_item":"Q59781882","titles":{"canonical":"Darren_Bailey","normalized":"Darren Bailey","display":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Darren Bailey</span></span>"},"pageid":59103874,"thumbnail":{"source":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7c/Darren_Bailey_at_a_2022_Campaign_Event_%28cropped2%29.jpg/330px-Darren_Bailey_at_a_2022_Campaign_Event_%28cropped2%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","width":330,"height":440},"originalimage":{"source":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/7/7c/Darren_Bailey_at_a_2022_Campaign_Event_%28cropped2%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","width":364,"height":485},"lang":"en","dir":"ltr","revision":"1376672917","tid":"e1365fc8-b8f9-11f1-95d8-d1e6892ec89c","timestamp":"2026-09-25T15:57:59Z","description":"American politician (born 1966)","description_source":"local","content_urls":{"desktop":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Darren_Bailey","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Darren_Bailey?action=history","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Darren_Bailey?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Darren_Bailey"},"mobile":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Darren_Bailey","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:History/Darren_Bailey","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Darren_Bailey?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Darren_Bailey"}},"extract":"Darren Bailey is an American politician who was a Republican member of the Illinois Senate for the 55th District and previously a member of the Illinois House of Representatives for the 109th District in Southern Illinois. Widely described by news outlets as a far-right politician, he was the Republican nominee for the 2022 Illinois gubernatorial election, losing to Democrat JB Pritzker. Bailey is once again the Republican nominee in the 2026 election.","extract_html":"<p><b>Darren Bailey</b> is an American politician who was a Republican member of the Illinois Senate for the 55th District and previously a member of the Illinois House of Representatives for the 109th District in Southern Illinois. Widely described by news outlets as a far-right politician, he was the Republican nominee for the 2022 Illinois gubernatorial election, losing to Democrat JB Pritzker. Bailey is once again the Republican nominee in the 2026 election.</p>"}